WEBVTT

00:00.626 --> 00:01.908
- [Instructor] In a video game,

00:01.908 --> 00:06.097
Val scored 30% fewer points than Peeta.

00:06.097 --> 00:08.264
Peeta scored 1,060 points.

00:09.553 --> 00:12.003
How many points did Val score?

00:12.003 --> 00:14.148
Pause this video and see
if you can figure out

00:14.148 --> 00:16.398
how many points Val scored.

00:17.396 --> 00:19.381
Alright, now let's do this together.

00:19.381 --> 00:21.491
And there's a couple of ways
that you could think about it.

00:21.491 --> 00:25.874
One way to think about is
Peeta scored 1,060 points,

00:25.874 --> 00:28.236
and Val scored 30% fewer.

00:28.236 --> 00:30.601
When we're saying 30% fewer,

00:30.601 --> 00:33.751
we're saying essentially take 30% of 1060

00:33.751 --> 00:36.016
and subtract that from 1060.

00:36.016 --> 00:40.183
So 30%, so we could write
that as a decimal as 0.30.

00:41.788 --> 00:45.652
30/100 is the same thing as 30%,

00:45.652 --> 00:48.611
or we could even write this as .3.

00:48.611 --> 00:51.944
And then we would want 30% of 1060.

00:53.198 --> 00:55.076
So if you take Peeta's score

00:55.076 --> 00:57.702
and then subtract 30% of Peeta's score,

00:57.702 --> 00:59.469
then this would give you Val's score.

00:59.469 --> 01:01.486
So that's one way to calculate it.

01:01.486 --> 01:03.469
Another way to think about is

01:03.469 --> 01:06.688
whatever you're starting
with, let's call that 100%,

01:06.688 --> 01:08.985
and if you were to take out 30% of it,

01:08.985 --> 01:10.868
if you were to have 30% less,

01:10.868 --> 01:14.423
then you're going to have
70% of what you started with.

01:14.423 --> 01:15.765
So another way to think about it is

01:15.765 --> 01:19.932
we could take Peeta's score of
1060 and multiply it by 70%.

01:22.490 --> 01:25.278
And multiplying it by
70% is the same thing

01:25.278 --> 01:27.445
as multiplying it by 0.70,

01:28.870 --> 01:32.529
which is the same thing as
multiplying it by 70/100,

01:32.529 --> 01:35.065
is the same thing as 7/10.

01:35.065 --> 01:36.487
So let's just do this.

01:36.487 --> 01:39.904
So if I have 1060, and I multiply by 0.7,

01:42.097 --> 01:43.322
what do I get?

01:43.322 --> 01:44.975
Seven times zero is zero.

01:44.975 --> 01:46.808
Seven times six is 42.

01:48.163 --> 01:51.225
Seven times zero is
zero, plus four is four.

01:51.225 --> 01:53.187
Seven times one is seven.

01:53.187 --> 01:55.803
And I have one digit to
the right of the decimal.

01:55.803 --> 01:58.470
So there you have it, it is 742.

02:00.778 --> 02:01.611
742.

02:03.234 --> 02:05.860
That is how many points Val scored.

02:05.860 --> 02:07.943
Let's do another example.

02:10.083 --> 02:13.238
So we're told there are 20% more goblins

02:13.238 --> 02:15.951
than wizards in a magic club.

02:15.951 --> 02:20.118
There are 220 goblins and
wizards altogether in magic club.

02:21.263 --> 02:25.166
How many goblins are in the magic club?

02:25.166 --> 02:26.833
So pause the video and see

02:26.833 --> 02:30.158
if you can work through this on your own.

02:30.158 --> 02:31.949
So this one is an interesting one.

02:31.949 --> 02:34.853
It's gonna involve a
little bit of algebra here.

02:34.853 --> 02:36.968
So what we wanna do is
let's set a variable.

02:36.968 --> 02:40.410
Let's say w is the number of wizards.

02:40.410 --> 02:42.533
So that's the number of wizards.

02:42.533 --> 02:46.700
And then if we said g for
goblins, let's say g for goblins.

02:47.634 --> 02:49.967
So w plus g is equal to 220,

02:52.866 --> 02:54.737
is equal to 220.

02:54.737 --> 02:56.479
And you're like, well,
how does that help me?

02:56.479 --> 02:58.422
How does that help me actually figure out

02:58.422 --> 03:00.334
how many goblins are in the magic club?

03:00.334 --> 03:03.047
I have two variables
here with one equation.

03:03.047 --> 03:04.805
Well, one way to think about it is,

03:04.805 --> 03:06.566
remember, they give us
some more information.

03:06.566 --> 03:09.973
They tell us there are
20%, let me box that,

03:09.973 --> 03:13.770
there are 20% more goblins than wizards.

03:13.770 --> 03:15.900
So we also know one other thing.

03:15.900 --> 03:19.887
We know that the goblins,
we know that the goblins

03:19.887 --> 03:24.415
are equal to the number
of wizards plus 20%.

03:24.415 --> 03:27.165
So you could view this as wizards

03:28.014 --> 03:30.836
plus 20% of wizards.

03:30.836 --> 03:32.609
And I'm writing that as 20/100,

03:32.609 --> 03:34.751
or you could even write that as 2/10,

03:34.751 --> 03:37.793
plus 2/10 times the number of wizards.

03:37.793 --> 03:39.491
Or another way of thinking about it,

03:39.491 --> 03:42.728
goblins are equal to, if
I have one of something

03:42.728 --> 03:44.964
and then I have another
2/10 of that something,

03:44.964 --> 03:48.297
then I'm gonna have 1.2 of that something.

03:48.297 --> 03:52.047
So goblins is equal to
1.2 times the wizards.

03:53.006 --> 03:57.754
And so we could use that
to substitute back in here,

03:57.754 --> 04:00.557
and then we could say
the number of wizards

04:00.557 --> 04:04.724
plus the number of goblins,
which happens to be 20% more

04:05.742 --> 04:09.909
than the number of wizards,
is going to be equal to 220.

04:12.031 --> 04:13.618
Let me do that in that same color.

04:13.618 --> 04:15.275
Is equal to 220.

04:15.275 --> 04:18.067
Now this is pretty
straightforward to solve.

04:18.067 --> 04:19.734
What is w plus 1.2w?

04:20.811 --> 04:24.373
Well, that is going to be 2.2w, 2.2w.

04:24.373 --> 04:27.793
You could view this as one w plus 1.2w

04:27.793 --> 04:29.793
is 2.2w is equal to 220.

04:32.547 --> 04:34.639
And so just divide both sides.

04:34.639 --> 04:36.005
Let me scroll down a little bit.

04:36.005 --> 04:38.505
Divide both sides by 2.2, 2.2,

04:40.047 --> 04:41.664
and what do you get?

04:41.664 --> 04:45.414
You get w, the number
of wizards is equal to,

04:47.146 --> 04:50.169
let's see, this is going
to be equal to 100.

04:50.169 --> 04:52.384
The number of wizards is equal to 100.

04:52.384 --> 04:53.887
Now is that our answer?

04:53.887 --> 04:58.600
No, they're asking how many
goblins are in the magic club?

04:58.600 --> 05:02.370
Well, we know that goblins
are 1.2 times the wizards.

05:02.370 --> 05:06.537
So the number of goblins is
going to be 1.2 times 100,

05:08.246 --> 05:10.670
which is equal to 120.

05:10.670 --> 05:13.446
So there's 120 goblins,
does that make sense?

05:13.446 --> 05:16.633
120 is 20% more than 100.

05:16.633 --> 05:19.457
And if you add the 100
wizards to the 120 goblins,

05:19.457 --> 05:23.627
you get 220 goblins
and wizards altogether.

05:23.627 --> 05:26.087
Let's do another example.

05:26.087 --> 05:30.486
Here we're told Cody
was 165 centimeters tall

05:30.486 --> 05:32.414
on the first day of school this year,

05:32.414 --> 05:34.506
which was 10% taller than he was

05:34.506 --> 05:37.362
on the first day of school last year.

05:37.362 --> 05:42.096
How tall was Cody on the
first day of school last year?

05:42.096 --> 05:46.206
Pause this video, see if
you can figure that out.

05:46.206 --> 05:47.930
So let's just define a variable here.

05:47.930 --> 05:50.877
Let's just say that his
height on the first day

05:50.877 --> 05:54.660
of school last year,
let's say that that is x.

05:54.660 --> 05:58.069
So his height on the first
day of school last year is x.

05:58.069 --> 06:00.627
This year he is 10% taller,

06:00.627 --> 06:04.368
so we would add 10%, which
we could say is 10/100,

06:04.368 --> 06:07.174
or we could even say that as 1/10.

06:07.174 --> 06:09.262
He's 1/10 taller.

06:09.262 --> 06:11.272
So whatever his height was last year,

06:11.272 --> 06:14.068
we're going to add 1/10
of that same height again

06:14.068 --> 06:15.710
to get to his height this year,

06:15.710 --> 06:19.578
which they tell us is 165 centimeters.

06:19.578 --> 06:23.893
And so here we could say
well, one x plus 1/10 of an x

06:23.893 --> 06:28.060
is going to be one and
1/10x is equal to 165.

06:29.121 --> 06:31.265
And now to solve for x, which
remember, was his height

06:31.265 --> 06:33.490
on the first day of school last year,

06:33.490 --> 06:35.823
we divide both sides by 1.1.

06:36.693 --> 06:38.529
And so x is equal to,

06:38.529 --> 06:40.402
well, let's see what this is going to be.

06:40.402 --> 06:43.485
If I were to take 165 divided by 1.1,

06:46.153 --> 06:48.580
the first thing I would wanna do

06:48.580 --> 06:51.171
is multiply them both by 10.

06:51.171 --> 06:53.216
So that has the effect of moving

06:53.216 --> 06:55.786
this decimal place one to the right.

06:55.786 --> 06:57.632
So really, I am now trying to figure out

06:57.632 --> 06:59.882
what 11 goes into 1,650 is.

07:02.401 --> 07:05.230
And so let's see, let me
just do that step by step.

07:05.230 --> 07:08.080
11 goes into 16 one time.

07:08.080 --> 07:09.885
One times 11 is 11.

07:09.885 --> 07:13.860
Subtract, we get a five,
and we bring down a five.

07:13.860 --> 07:16.480
11 goes into 55 exactly five times.

07:16.480 --> 07:18.643
Five times 11 is 55.

07:18.643 --> 07:20.041
Subtract.

07:20.041 --> 07:22.691
We have no remainder, but
then we bring down this zero

07:22.691 --> 07:23.721
and we do it one more time.

07:23.721 --> 07:25.924
11 goes into zero zero times.

07:25.924 --> 07:28.459
Remember, the decimal
place is right over here.

07:28.459 --> 07:31.455
Zero times 11 is zero, and
then we have no remainder.

07:31.455 --> 07:35.010
So last year he was 150 centimeters.

07:35.010 --> 07:37.027
And it's always good
to do a reality check.

07:37.027 --> 07:38.909
Make sure, if for example,
if I divided wrong

07:38.909 --> 07:41.504
and I somehow got 15, or I got 1500,

07:41.504 --> 07:43.689
just to make sure that that
wouldn't make any sense.

07:43.689 --> 07:46.539
150 centimeters, you add 10% of that.

07:46.539 --> 07:49.467
10% of 150 is 15 centimeters.

07:49.467 --> 07:52.068
So you add 10% of that, you indeed do get

07:52.068 --> 07:56.235
to 165 centimeters for the
first day of school this year.
